>Belknap:
>> >By the way, has lojban central managed to get any reviews by the mainstream
>> >press, linguistics journals, or logic journals?
>
>Lojbab:
>> No we have not
>
>Why not? Isn't anyone interested in the Sapir-Whorf hypothesis?

Simply speaking, within the academic linguistics community - no.
Anthropologists still consider it an interesting and open question, but
until Chomsky has been displaced, S/W will be on the outs in linguistic
academia.

There are of course individual linguists still interested in S/W, but they
by and large do not publish on the topic.

